referrer noopener\"><img alt=\"https://bg3.norbyte.dev/search?q=uuid:684f64c6-ce63-4db0-b702-5c6f45756156\" src=\"/w/images/7/70/Search_icon.svg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></a></span></span></li></ul>\n</div>   \n<div style=\"clear: both;\"></div></div>\n    <h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Where_to_find\"> Where to find </span></h2>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-tooltip-box\">\n<ul><li>Carried by <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Mirie\" title=\"Mirie\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/19/Portrait_Mirie.png/25px-Portrait_Mirie.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/19/Portrait_Mirie.png/38px-Portrait_Mirie.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/19/Portrait_Mirie.png/50px-Portrait_Mirie.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Mirie\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/19/Portrait_Mirie.png/25px-Portrait_Mirie.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/1/19/Portrait_Mirie.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Mirie\" title=\"Mirie\">Mirie</a> in the <a href=\"/wiki/House_of_Grief\" title=\"House of Grief\">House of Grief</a></li></ul>\n</div>  <h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Text\"> Text </span></h2>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-book-text\">\n<p>[A self-help tome, boasting means of moving past inclinations towards nosiness and interfering with others.]\n</p><p><br>\n</p><p>To become involved in the lives of others is a simple fact of life, but what if you become too involved? To vicariously sup upon the joys, sadnesses and secrets of those around yourself points to a sickening emptiness in the heart. You must fill it with life and feeling of your own, even if it hurts you. Even if it poisons you. Otherwise, you will remain an empty vessel. \n</p><p><br>\n</p><p>[The book continues on at great length, suggesting treatments pioneered by the House of Grief may help, should self-improvement fail.]\n</p>\n</div>    \n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260715013547\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [vary‐revision‐sha1, no‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.053 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.056 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1888/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 32169/4194304 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 8630/4194304 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 29/200\nExpensive parser function count: 3/750\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2/5000000 bytes\nExtLoops count: 0/1000\nLua time usage: 0.011/7.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 931825/52428800 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   44.142      1 Template:MiscItemPage\n100.00%   44.142      1 -total\n 55.28%   24.400      8 Template:Icon_text\n 48.39%   21.362     19 Template:Trim\n 21.10%    9.314      2 Template:Uid\n 15.19%    6.704      3 Template:Icon_link\n 14.54%    6.416      1 Template:Main_only\n 12.12%    5.352      2 Template:Template_style\n 10.95%    4.835      1 Template:PageSeo\n 10.72%    4.730      2 Template:Hidden_code\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key bg3wiki:pcache:idhash:43669-0!canonical and timestamp 20260715013547 and revision id 322079. Rendering was triggered because: unknown\n -->\n</div>"}